.TH APT-FIND-REPO 1 "December 2024" "apt-find-repo 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
apt-find-repo \- find and add third-party APT repositories from web pages
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B apt-find-repo
[\fB\-v\fR]
.I url
[\fBadd\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B apt-find-repo
parses web pages that describe third-party Debian/Ubuntu repositories,
extracts GPG signing keys and source list entries, and lists available
packages. When invoked with the \fBadd\fR argument, it installs the
repository configuration to the system.
.PP
The tool automates the manual process of reading repository documentation,
downloading GPG keys, and creating sources.list entries. It generates modern
deb822 format sources files in \fI/etc/apt/sources.list.d/\fR and stores
keys in \fI/etc/apt/keyrings/\fR.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-v
Verbose output. Shows GPG key URLs, source entries, and installation progress
on stderr.
.TP
.I url
URL of a web page containing repository installation instructions, such as
a GitHub README or documentation page.
.TP
.B add
Install the repository. Requires root privileges. Without this argument,
the command only lists available packages.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Detect a repository and list available packages:
.PP
.nf
.RS
apt-find-repo https://github.com/JonasGroeger/jetbrains-ppa
.RE
.fi
.PP
Install the detected repository (requires root):
.PP
.nf
.RS
sudo apt-find-repo https://github.com/JonasGroeger/jetbrains-ppa add
.RE
.fi
.PP
Show detailed information about what was found:
.PP
.nf
.RS
apt-find-repo -v https://github.com/JonasGroeger/jetbrains-ppa
.RE
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/apt/keyrings/*.gpg
.TQ
.I /etc/apt/keyrings/*.asc
GPG signing keys for third-party repositories. Keys are stored in binary
(.gpg) or ASCII-armored (.asc) format depending on the source format.
.TP
.I /etc/apt/sources.list.d/*.sources
Repository source entries in deb822 format. Files are named after the
repository.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success
.TP
.B 1
Error occurred (missing keys, missing sources, permission denied, etc.)
.SH NOTES
The tool requires root privileges (via \fBsudo\fR) when invoked with the
\fBadd\fR argument to write system configuration files.
.PP
Repository keys and sources are validated before installation. If a key or
sources file already exists at the target location, the command will fail
rather than overwrite existing configuration.
.PP
After adding a repository, run \fBapt update\fR to refresh the package cache:
.PP
.nf
.RS
sudo apt update
.RE
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR apt (8),
.BR apt-key (8),
.BR sources.list (5)
